In versions of (Advanced )?Dungeons and Dragons prior to the release of
Third Edition D&D, certain monsters are completely immune to weapons
below a certain level of enchantment.  This includes greater devils,
greater demons, elementals, werefoo (though werefoos can also be hurt
by silver weapons) and pretty much any undead monster more powerful
than a ghoul or ghast (though again, some of those can be harmed by
silver).

In Third Edition, this mechanic was replaced with "Damage Reduction";
monsters with Damage Reduction reduce all damage from physical attacks
by a certain amount unless the attack meets the necessary criteria.  For
example, a monster with 20/silver Damage Reduction takes 20 points less
damage from physical attacks unless made with a silver weapon, a weapon
with a positive magical bonus, or by another monster with xx/silver or
xx/(enchantment-level) Damage Reduction.

In practice, doing 21 points of damage with a single attack is very
hard, but definitely not impossible.
